From: Douglas Teles <dga.teles@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: px30: list the GPU rates the clock can make

clk_gpu is gpll (1200MHz) through an integer divider or a half divider,
so the 560MHz OPP ran at 480MHz with 560's voltage, and the 650MHz turbo
OPP at 600MHz: devfreq reported rates the GPU never ran at and scaled
its load from them. Measured on an R36S with the userspace governor:

  requested 560MHz -> clk_gpu 480MHz, vdd_logic 1.125V
  requested 650MHz -> clk_gpu 600MHz, vdd_logic 1.15V

The 560 step now says 480MHz, at the voltage it already ran at, and 650
is disabled (a second OPP at 600MHz would fail the whole table). The
node names stay, since the boot tuning overlay addresses steps by them.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/px30.dtsi	2026-11-23 08:16:04.854833690 -0300
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/px30.dtsi	2026-11-23 08:19:41.720344207 -0300
@@ -1413,8 +1413,16 @@
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <400000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <1100000>;
 		};
+		/*
+		 * clk_gpu comes from gpll (1200MHz) through an integer or a
+		 * half divider: 1200/n or 1200/(n+0.5) only. The stock 560MHz
+		 * ran at 480 and 650 at 600 (measured on an R36S), so this step
+		 * says 480, and 650 is off (two OPPs at 600 fail the table).
+		 * The node names stay: archr-boot-tuning's overlay addresses
+		 * the steps by them.
+		 */
 		opp-560000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <560000000>;
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <480000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <1125000>;
 		};
 		opp-600000000 {
@@ -1425,6 +1433,7 @@
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <650000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <1150000>;
 			turbo-mode;
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 	};
 
